From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS5 Mesa port <ps5-mesa@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:25:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] addrlib: the PS5's CPU has AVX2

addrlib picks its AVX2 copy routines with __builtin_cpu_supports(), which
reads compiler-rt's __cpu_model. The PS5 payload SDK links no compiler-rt,
so a shared library using addrlib does not link there. The console's Zen 2
cores always have AVX2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ZqjJDSiP9GQFUidfnxiHF
---
 src/amd/addrlib/src/core/addrswizzlersimd.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/amd/addrlib/src/core/addrswizzlersimd.h b/src/amd/addrlib/src/core/addrswizzlersimd.h
index fd53e4080a3..39dcb8829cf 100644
--- a/src/amd/addrlib/src/core/addrswizzlersimd.h
+++ b/src/amd/addrlib/src/core/addrswizzlersimd.h
@@ -84,6 +84,10 @@ static inline bool CpuSupportsAvx2() {
     // Use compiler builtins to check for support
 #if _MSC_VER
     return IsProcessorFeaturePresent(PF_AVX2_INSTRUCTIONS_AVAILABLE);
+#elif defined(__PROSPERO__)
+    // The PS5's Zen 2 cores have AVX2; and __builtin_cpu_supports() needs
+    // compiler-rt's __cpu_model, which the PS5 payload SDK does not link.
+    return true;
 #elif defined(__GNUC__)
     return __builtin_cpu_supports("avx2");
 #else
